WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys,
I'm excited about this.

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:04.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
Super Bowl LIII is on Sunday.
Oh, yeah.

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which means we're just
a few days away

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
from your drunk friend
walking in front of the TV

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.343 size:75% position:38% line:92%
at a crucial moment.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.312 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Damn it, Ryan!"

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:13.213 line:92%
I do, I love the Super Bowl.

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every year, I watch the game
on a 100-inch TV,

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:19.085
until the Best Buy manager says,
"Sir, we need you to leave."

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.588 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:25.425
I saw that, on Sunday,
a 30-second ad costs $5 million.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.092 size:75% position:38% line:92%
[ Audience murmurs ]

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, but it will be worth it
when people are watching,

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:29.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, "Oh, yeah,
I totally forgot

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
about Amazon, Bud Light,
and Google."

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.332 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:36.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
So smart that --
You need to advertise more.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's right,
$5 million for 30 seconds.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:39.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
The president said,
"That's crazy.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
30 seconds
only costs me $130,000."

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:46.179 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:49.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
But $5 million really is a lot
for a 30-second commercial,

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:52.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
which might explain the
Super Bowl ad I saw for Sears.

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.254 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Watch this.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:55.155 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sears.

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:56.890 line:92%
We're not just a department --

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:57.857 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Ah.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:58.391 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.627
That's all they could afford.
-That's all they could afford?

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's all they could --
They couldn't do it.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-I get it now.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.499 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.334 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Short ad.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it gets
the message out there.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:10.403 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I saw that Americans
are expected to bet $6 billion

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.075 line:92%
on the Super Bowl this year.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the bets aren't just
for the game itself.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:18.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can bet
on all sorts of things.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:18.812 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I'll show what I mean.

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:21.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
For example, first up,
the odds are 7-1

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
that everyone
stays late drinking

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:25.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
at your Super Bowl party
on Sunday night.

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:25.885 size:78% position:39% line:92%
The odds are also 7-1

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:29.255
that your boss believes you have
the flu on Monday morning.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.990 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"I'm sick."
-"A little sick."

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:36.229
Next up, the odds are 3-1 that
the halftime show goes long.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:39.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
The odds are also 3-1 that
your dad asks what the deal is

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:41.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
with that lit,
new band Maroon 7.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.204 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:48.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"I like their beat.
I like their beat a lot."

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:51.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Up next, the odds are 2-1
that the Patriots win,

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.278 line:92%
and the odds also are 2-1

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Gronk yells,
"I'm going to Disney World,"

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.182 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
even if they lose.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:59.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's a fun guy.
-Yeah.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:00.286 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, you guys,

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
the president's State
of the Union is on Tuesday,

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:06.159
and I saw that Stacey Abrams is
giving the Democratic rebuttal,

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:06.793 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and this is very nice --

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:09.295 size:78% position:39%
Joe Kennedy, who gave
last year's rebuttal,

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:10.063 size:78% position:39% line:92%
tweeted out some tips

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
and told her to,
"Just be yourself,"

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:14.667
and he's not the only Democrat
giving her advice on her speech.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
For example,
here's Senator Cory Booker.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
He told her, "If you get
nervous, just do what I do --

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:21.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tell people you're
The Rock's younger brother."

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.276 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:24.210 line:92%
Here's Congressman Eliot Engel.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said, "If you get nervous,
just do what I do --

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:27.680 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Picture everyone naked.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do that even when
I'm not giving a speech."

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.986 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:36.656 size:81% position:41%
Next up is Congressman
Dutch Ruppersberger.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said, "If you get nervous,
just do what I do --

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
Say the name
'Dutch Ruppersberger'

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:41.628 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and have a good laugh."

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:43.863 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here's the last one.
It's Congressman Jamie Raskin.

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:47.700 line:92%
He said, "If you get nervous,

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.304 size:81% position:41%
just do what I do with
my hair -- Let it go."

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
So nice.
-Wow.

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:53.206 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So nice of all --

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Kind. Very kind advice.
Very kind.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Finally, I heard about
a man in Arizona

00:02:56.442 --> 00:03:01.381
who just set a world record
by stacking 353 Jenga blocks.

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.081 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Or, as one guy put it,

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:04.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
[as President Trump]
"Maybe he can build a wall."

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:07.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a great show tonight.
Give it up for The Roots.

